Z||000000||mrgone||05-20-2001||03:05 PM||||well,the button wont go down on my ebrake lever, i tried kicking it, swearing at it, and crying.<P>can i loosen the e brake ajustment thing all the way?<P>i hate my car||||reg||8
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-20-2001||08:09 PM||||Yes, you can slacken the cables enough to where you can drive it.  Just loosen the e-brake equalizer nut until the cables are slack enough that the brake shoes will disengage.  After that, take off your lower trim and the ebrake boot and see what is up with your lever.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||05-20-2001||09:01 PM||||I had that problem on my 84 after redoing the rear brakes. It only happened if I pulled it up real far. If I would pull it a little further and push down on the button at the same time, it would release. Be careful not to pull so hard something breaks, like a cable. I learned it was not necessary to pull so far.<BR>Don||||reg||1
